 "facts": [
  {
   "claim": "The Judgement of Cambyses by Gerard David (c. 1460–1523), dated 1498 (the date is painted on the arrest panel); oil on oak, two panels, 182.3 × 318.6 cm overall",
   "source": "https://www.museabrugge.be/en/collection/work/id/0000_gro0040_i-0041_i ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Judgement_of_Cambyses"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Commissioned by the Bruges municipal authorities for the town hall; the aldermen saw it daily, a reminder to be incorruptible and fair (hung as 'justice panels' in the city hall)",
   "source": "https://www.museabrugge.be/en/collection/work/id/0000_gro0040_i-0041_i ; https://vlaamseprimitieven.vlaamsekunstcollectie.be/en/collection/judgement-of-cambyses/ ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Judgement_of_Cambyses"
  },
  {
   "claim": "The story comes from Herodotus, Histories 5.25: Sisamnes, a royal judge, took a bribe to give an unjust judgment",
   "source": "https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.01.0126:book=5:chapter=25 ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sisamnes"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Herodotus: Cambyses 'had cut his throat and flayed off all his skin' (Godley transl.) — killed, then skinned",
   "source": "https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.01.0126:book=5:chapter=25"
  },
  {
   "claim": "David's right panel shows Sisamnes being flayed alive on a table, four executioners at work (the leg already stripped); the background of the left panel shows Sisamnes accepting the bribe",
   "source": "https://vlaamseprimitieven.vlaamsekunstcollectie.be/en/collection/judgement-of-cambyses/ ; https://www.worldhistory.org/image/3244/the-judgement-of-cambyses-david/ ; https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gerard_David_-_The_Judgment_of_Cambyses,_panel_2_-_The_shedding_of_the_corrupt_judge_Sisamnes.jpg"
  },
  {
   "claim": "David set the scene as if it took place in Bruges in his own time (contemporary buildings and dress)",
   "source": "https://www.museabrugge.be/en/collection/work/id/0000_gro0040_i-0041_i ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sisamnes"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Herodotus: Cambyses cut leather strips from the skin and covered the seat Sisamnes had judged from",
   "source": "https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.01.0126:book=5:chapter=25"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Cambyses appointed Sisamnes' son (Otanes) judge in his place, 'admonishing him to keep in mind the nature of the throne on which he was sitting'",
   "source": "https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.01.0126:book=5:chapter=25"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Upper right of the flaying panel: the son, Otanes, sits as judge on the chair draped with his father's skin",
   "source": "https://vlaamseprimitieven.vlaamsekunstcollectie.be/en/collection/judgement-of-cambyses/ ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Judgement_of_Cambyses"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Hangs in the Groeningemuseum, Bruges (inv. 0000.GRO0040.I-0041.I)",
   "source": "https://www.museabrugge.be/en/collection/work/id/0000_gro0040_i-0041_i"
  },
  {
   "claim": "(caption P.S.) In August 2012 Yulia Tymoshenko's supporters showed a reproduction of the painting to the judge reviewing her case",
   "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Judgement_of_Cambyses (citing Lenta.ru, 16 Aug 2012)"
  }
 ],
 "caption": "Every judge in Bruges had to look at this.\n\nIn 1498 Gerard David finished two huge panels for the Bruges town hall. The story comes from Herodotus: Sisamnes, a royal judge in Persia, took a bribe to give an unjust verdict, and King Cambyses had him killed and skinned. David paints him alive, tied to a table, while four men peel away his skin, and dresses the whole crowd like the people of Bruges in his own day.\n\nHerodotus says the skin was cut into strips and laid over the judge's seat. Then the king named a new judge: the dead man's own son, told to remember what he was sitting on. Look at the top right corner of the panel: there he is, on his father's skin.\n\nThe aldermen of Bruges saw it every day, as a warning to stay honest.\n\nP.S. In 2012 Yulia Tymoshenko's supporters showed a copy of this painting to the judge reviewing her case.\n\n🖤 Would you take a bribe under this painting?",
 "caption_short": "Every judge in Bruges had to look at this: a corrupt judge skinned, and his son made to sit on the skin. 🖤",
 "youtube_title": "What is his chair made of? Gerard David's Judgement of Cambyses",
